<workout_file>
    <author>Coach Claude</author>
    <name>3x12 Threshold — 188W</name>
    <description>Wed Aug 26 PM. SET FTP TO 185. 3x12min at 188W, 4min recoveries.

SET AT THE TOP OF THE BAND (180-190W) ON PURPOSE. Two sessions now say your ceiling is above 185: the Aug 20 test held 4x8min at 185W with max HR 149, and Aug 23 held 45min CONTINUOUS at 159W with max HR 143. Neither of those is a rider at their limit.

RECORD RPE PER BLOCK. That is the output of this session, same as the FTP test. If 188W reads 6-7/10 across all three, next Wednesday goes to 198-200W and race power moves up with it - which makes the sub-5 bike split materially easier.

EAT FIRST. You ran 8x400m this morning. 40-60g carbs at least 30min before you start.

HIDE THE HEART RATE FIELD. Watts and RPE only.

SIM IS SUNDAY, not Saturday - so this sits 4 days out and can be a real session. Do not sandbag it.

AERO where you can. Not required on the threshold blocks if it costs you power, but the Z2 block after should be in the bars.

AFTER: 75-90g carb + 30-40g protein within 60min.</description>
    <sportType>bike</sportType>
    <tags>
        <tag name="threshold"/>
        <tag name="703"/>
    </tags>
    <workout>
        <Warmup Duration="960" PowerLow="0.50" PowerHigh="0.75" Cadence="90">
            <textevent timeoffset="10" message="80min: 16 warmup, 3x12min at 188W, 4min recoveries, 12min Z2"/>
            <textevent timeoffset="40" message="Did you eat? Track this morning - you need carbs on board"/>
            <textevent timeoffset="240" message="HIDE THE HR FIELD. Watts and RPE only"/>
            <textevent timeoffset="660" message="Spin-up 1: 30s at 105rpm, same power"/>
            <textevent timeoffset="780" message="Spin-up 2: 30s at 105rpm"/>
            <textevent timeoffset="890" message="Settle. Block 1 next. 188W - a touch above the last test"/>
        </Warmup>

        <SteadyState Duration="720" Power="1.016" Cadence="90">
            <textevent timeoffset="10" message="Block 1 of 3: 12min at 188W"/>
            <textevent timeoffset="360" message="Halfway. Note the RPE - it decides next week's target"/>
            <textevent timeoffset="660" message="1min left. Smooth to the line"/>
        </SteadyState>
        <SteadyState Duration="240" Power="0.55" Cadence="85">
            <textevent timeoffset="10" message="4min easy. RPE for block 1? Remember it"/>
            <textevent timeoffset="150" message="Drink"/>
        </SteadyState>

        <SteadyState Duration="720" Power="1.016" Cadence="90">
            <textevent timeoffset="10" message="Block 2 of 3. Same 188W"/>
            <textevent timeoffset="360" message="Halfway. Higher than block 1? A little is normal"/>
            <textevent timeoffset="660" message="Final minute"/>
        </SteadyState>
        <SteadyState Duration="240" Power="0.55" Cadence="85">
            <textevent timeoffset="10" message="4min easy. Eat. One to go"/>
        </SteadyState>

        <SteadyState Duration="720" Power="1.016" Cadence="90">
            <textevent timeoffset="10" message="Block 3 of 3. This is the one that sets next week"/>
            <textevent timeoffset="360" message="Halfway. Still 6-7/10? Then 200W next Wednesday"/>
            <textevent timeoffset="660" message="Final minute. Finish it"/>
        </SteadyState>

        <SteadyState Duration="720" Power="0.72" Cadence="90">
            <textevent timeoffset="10" message="12min Z2 at 133W. GET IN THE BARS - free position time"/>
            <textevent timeoffset="400" message="Log the three RPE numbers before you forget them"/>
        </SteadyState>

        <Cooldown Duration="480" PowerLow="0.62" PowerHigh="0.45" Cadence="85">
            <textevent timeoffset="10" message="8min down"/>
            <textevent timeoffset="240" message="75-90g carb + 30-40g protein within the hour"/>
            <textevent timeoffset="420" message="Send me the RPEs and the average watts held"/>
        </Cooldown>
    </workout>
</workout_file>
